******************** Angular Modules***********************************
Angular module is a class decorated with @NgModule() meta data.
1.bootstrap:- every module must define atleast one component in bootstarp array, so that compiler will come to know where to start execution.
              and it should be defined only in root module, not in any child modules.
2.declarations:- All components, pipes , filters etc that are defined for the module must be registered inside declaration array.
                 All components, pipes etc defined in a module is private to that module. If any module that imports another module, can't use its components or pipes directly.
3.Exports:-  Any component/pipe that are declared in export array of 'A' module, will be available to 'B' module if 'B' module imports module 'A'.
4.Providers- All services are registerd here. We should add services only in root module in order to have Singleton design pattern.
             Once it is registered in main module , it is available through out the application.
	     Never export any service.
5.Imports:- All supporting modules can be imported in this array.


