**********************Lifecycle **********************************************
1.constructor
2.ngOnChanges:- this event fires when one or more propery value changes in DOM. This event keeps info of both old & new value of 
                that property.
3.ngOnInit:- fires after ngOnChange. This event initializes property value of component or directive once the default value of 
              all properties gets initialized. it is called only once.
4.ngDoCheck:- Detect and act upon changes that Angular can't or won't detect on its own. fires after ngOnChanges & ngOnInit.
5.ngAfterContentInit:- this event fires when angular tries to put external content into a view.
6.ngAfterContentChecked:- Respond after Angular checks the content projected into the component.
7.ngAfterViewInit:- Respond after Angular initializes the component's views and child views.
8.ngAfterViewChecked:- Respond after Angular checks the component's views and child views.
9.ngOndestroy:- Cleanup just before Angular destroys the directive/component.  Unsubscribe Observables and detach event handlers 
                to avoid memory leaks. Called just before Angular destroys the directive/component.


